STATEMENT: >>>
Grammar to load: `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-python` (nixpkgs, 0.25.0, `python313Packages`/`python314Packages` binding present). This is also the grammar strictdoc's own built-in `reader_python.py` uses natively (source traceability, gated off in this repo today), so a repo-side extractor and strictdoc's own reader would target the same grammar.

Candidate items (node type, confirmed against upstream `tree-sitter/tree-sitter-python`'s `src/node-types.json`): `function_definition`, `class_definition`, `decorated_definition` (a `@decorator` wrapping either of the first two — strictdoc's own reader treats this as its own top-level case).

Present in this repo today: 75 files, the largest non-Nix, non-Markdown language by tracked-file count — the `dev/scripts/` tooling (scribe, the sdoc extractors, checks) and `checks/*.py`.

Gap: none noted. No dialect ambiguity, and the grammar is already proven inside this exact toolchain via strictdoc's bundled reader.
